*.hex
*.o
*.elf
*.DS_Store
*.d

build/
build_*/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generated by tools/gen_compile_commands.py - machine-specific absolute
# paths, regenerate with `make -C grbl/platform/<platform> compdb`.
compile_commands.json

README.md

# The repo-wide `README.md` ignore rule above matches README.md in any
# directory; explicitly un-ignore this one so it can be tracked.
!tools/README.md

# Every grbl/platform/<name>/README.md is a real, tracked porting doc
# (samd21, stm32f103, sg2002, ... already are - this just makes the
# existing convention explicit) - including grbl/platform/_template/'s,
# whose whole point is to be copied into every new port's directory. Without
# this, `git add` on a freshly copied _template/ silently drops its README.
!grbl/platform/*/README.md

# SAME TRAP, one more time: artifacts/README.md documents the tracked
# build-artifact tree (PLAN.md "build artifacts tracked in git" batch) and
# is a real, tracked doc like the two exceptions above - without this it
# silently vanishes from `git add -A` exactly like tools/README.md did
# before its own exception landed.
!artifacts/README.md

# SAME CLASS OF TRAP, caught before landing (Phase 6 rolling #4 review):
# grbl/platform/ch570/vendor/ISP572.o is a deliberately vendored, TRACKED
# binary (Apache-2.0, openwch/ch570 - LICENSE copied alongside in the same
# directory) - line 2's blanket `*.o` rule would otherwise silently drop
# it from every `git add -A`, exactly like the README.md rule above did
# for platform docs until that exception landed. This is the ONE
# vendored-binary exception in this tree; see CONTRACTS.md's CH570
# gap-log entry for why the flash program/erase algorithm is carried as a
# linked object instead of reimplemented (the vendor's own datasheet
# states it deliberately does not document the register protocol this
# function uses, and disassembly confirms real, non-trivial logic, not a
# thin trampoline). Verify with `git check-ignore -v` after ANY future
# .gitignore edit - a silent re-swallow here breaks every fresh clone's
# link, not just this session's build.
!grbl/platform/ch570/vendor/ISP572.o

# SAME CLASS OF TRAP again (PLAN.md "build artifacts tracked in git for
# observability" batch, owner directive): artifacts/<port>/*.elf and
# *.hex are deliberately TRACKED - RELEASE elf/bin/hex + a plain-text
# symbol-size map (.syms) per buildable port, so every port's CURRENT
# byte-level state is diffable over time (git log -p / git diff), not
# just AVR's golden MD5. Line 1's blanket `*.hex` and line 3's blanket
# `*.elf` would otherwise silently drop every one of them from `git add
# -A`, exactly like the README.md and ch570-vendor-.o exceptions above.
# .bin/.syms/MANIFEST.sha256 need no exception - no blanket rule above
# matches those extensions. See tools/build_artifacts.py and
# artifacts/README.md for what generates this tree and the refresh
# policy. Verify with `git check-ignore -v` after ANY future .gitignore
# edit - a silent re-swallow here breaks observability for every port at
# once, not just one.
!artifacts/**/*.elf
!artifacts/**/*.hex
